   "Job Description": "WordPress Developer\n\nVideojet Technologies, Inc.\nI.Company Specifics\nVideojet Technologies Inc.\nCompany President: Brad Ellis\nHiring Team Director: Mauro Mazzocchini\nHiring Manager: Sharath Suvarna\nPosition Location: Bhandup, Mumbai\nTotal Headcount (Videojet): Approximately 3,000\nAnnual Revenue: Approximately $900 million\nAnnual Profit: Profitable\nProduct Lines: Videojet is the leading provider of product and case coding solutions to a wide range of industries including food, beverage, pharmaceutical, personal care, electronics, chemical, and aerospace. Our Uptime Peace of Mind™ brand promise means Videojet listens to its customers’ needs and provides the right equipment, supplies and software combined for reliable performance.\nDistribution Channels: Videojet utilizes a combination of direct and indirect sales channels. The vast majority of all solutions are deployed by Videojet’s direct sales organization.\nII.Purpose of the Position\n\nThe WordPress Developer will be responsible for both back-end and front-end development of Videojet’s websites, including creating WordPress themes and plugins. He/she will have excellent programming skills and deep understanding of PHP, HTML5, CSS3, and JavaScript.\n\nThe candidate should have a strong understanding of industry trends and content management systems. Experience with the responsive and adaptive design is strongly preferred. Also, an understanding of the entire web development process, including design, development, and deployment is essential.\n\nRelationships\nReports to: Global Web Content Manager (Mumbai)\nKey Relationships:\nGlobal Automation Team and Web Content Team\nDirector of Digital Marketing\nDigital Marketing Specialists in each country\nIT Web Support team\n\nRequirements for the Position\nEducation – Degree educated with a strong professional experience (Computer Science/Software engineer graduate preferred).\n\nWork experience:\nA strong PHP & OOP background with WordPress experience (3+ years, including troubleshooting and debugging).\nExperience in developing custom WP plugins , modules, and themes (Ensure the new custom creations work properly in all environments while overcoming conflicts with popular themes and plugins)\nExperience and deep understanding of the WP library and other common practices to produce WP-based products\nExperience working with Responsive Landing Pages compatible with mobile and tablet designing\nKnowledge and experience working on MySQL database\nExperience of how to interact with RESTful APIs and formats (JSON, XML)\nExperience using version control software (VCS), preferably GIT, or at least SVN/Mercurial.\nExperience managing WP upgrades including testing and troubleshooting\nLight experience managing security, server migration, server management, etc.\nExperience with deploying via a CI (Continuous Integration) pipeline and specific experience on scaling WordPress sites for high traffic and large amounts of content.\n\nExperience working in a matrixed team organization and in a global environment\n\nSkills required :\nExpert knowledge of HTML, JavaScript, PHP. AJAX & MySQL, JSON format\nAbility to fully understand the website architecture\nKnowledge of WordPress hosting/dedicated hosting. ( ability to work with WordPress VIP’s command line interface to do task like search and replace in the database and understanding of VIP Go skeleton )\nAwareness or experience using a tool like xDebug / New Relic or similar\nGood understanding of Google Analytics & Search console to track the web traffic\n\nExcellent leadership and project management skills, ownership of the task\nExpertise in software development, product design, with good user experience instincts\nFluency in English – spoken and written\n\nLevel of travel required: Minimal (< 10%).\nV.Key Competencies (rank ordered)\nGood understanding of front-end technologies, including HTML, CSS, JavaScript, jQuery\nStrong understanding of PHP back-end development\nExperience building user interfaces for websites and/or web applications\nExperience designing and developing responsive design websites\nComfortable working with debugging tools like Firebug, Chrome inspector, etc.\nAbility to understand CSS changes and their ramifications to ensure consistent style across platforms and browsers\nAbility to convert comprehensive layout and wireframes into working HTML pages\nProficient understanding of code versioning tools {{such as Git, SVN or Mercurial}}\nExperience with marketing automation software Marketo / Pardot\nExcellent communication skills, writing skills, and project management skills (organizing, prioritizing and tracking all phases of a project).\nVI.Why Is This an Attractive Opportunity\nVideojet is rapidly expanding its internet marketing efforts and this position provides the opportunity to have significant and measurable impact on a highly respected, well-managed and fast-growing company.\nOpportunity to join fast-growing platform within Danaher."
