   "Job Title": "JavaScript Developer",
   "Job Description": "Company Description\n\nAbout BlueOptima\n\nBlueOptima provides industry-leading objective metrics in software development using our proprietary Coding Effort Analytics. We enable large organisations to deliver better software, faster and at a lower cost. Founded in 2006, BlueOptima is a profitable, high-growth independent software company. Our unique technology was initially devised in seminal research carried out at Cambridge University.\n\nOur HQ is in London, UK with 5 additional global offices in India, Mexico and the US.\n\nBlueOptima’s technology is deployed by global enterprises to drive value from their software development activities. We work with 12 of the Fortune 50 Companies, 4 of the top 10 biggest banks by Market Capital and 6 of the S&P 50 Companies (by revenue).\n\nOur technology is pushing the limits of complex analytics on large data-sets with more than 15 billion static source code metric observations of software engineers working in an Enterprise software development environment.\n\nJob Description\n\nProject Brief -\n\nTo identify security flaws by eyeballing in static C/C++/Javascript code and replicate them manually by morphing/editing/rewriting the code.\nRole -\n\nUnderstanding of the Security space should be able to understand CWEs, CVEs, CPEs\nAbility to run Penetration Tests and Static Analysers\nAdvanced programming ability in multiple languages\nNeedless to say, immaculate English communication skills both written and verbal\n\nAutomation Bounty:\n\nWe strongly believe that smart engineers are lazy and thus find ways to automate manual tasks effectively. We encourage you to be creative and come up with automated/semi-automated approaches to tag vulnerabilities accurately.\n\nThe developer who reduces project time and manual effort the maximum while keeping the accuracy intact is going to be rewarded handsomely.\n\nNote: The bounty program is subject to a minimum threshold. Overall project time and manual effort should be reduced by a minimum of 50% to be eligible for the prize.\n\nProgramming Languages in Scope\n\nC\nC++\nJavascript\n\nQualifications\n\nnull\n\nAdditional Information\n\nLocation- Remote\n\nIt's a freelancing role! Please don't apply if you are looking for Full-Time Employment!"
