   "Job Title": "Software Engineer",
   "Job Description": "\n\nJob Summary: We are looking for highly skilled Java/Python/Scala/UI developers to implement coding in Cienas NextGen NMS system i.e BluePlanet MCP. BluePlanet MCP is Cienas domain controller, automating lifecycle operations of Cienas packet and optical networks. Based on Microservices architecture, MCP helps network operators to Plan, provision, and turn up multi-layer services quickly using a highly intuitive interface. MCP marks a strategic shift from legacy network management software, enabling the transformation to open, scalable software control that easily integrates into network operators Billing and Operations Support Systems (B/OSS) and Orchestration layers using open REST APIs.\n\nRoles and Responsibilities: As a software developer, you would be involved in following\nUnderstanding of requirements from Product Owners/Architects representing various domains and components of MCP\nWorking on HLD/LLD of the MCP Release features\nQuick Prototyping using newer technologies and open source platforms in Web and NMS domains\nCoding various components of BluePlanet MCP Software in Java/Scala/Python/UI\nCreate Automated Test Suites for executing test automation of your features\nTroubleshooting product issues found in System Integration Testing and Customer deployments.\nMandatory skills:\n3+ years of Software Development Experience in Python/UI involving Web Technologies.\nExcellent understanding of Data Structures and Multi-threading concepts.\nExcellent troubleshooting/debugging skills.\nExcellent Problem-Solving skills.\nExcellent Communications skills.\nPreferred Skills:\nWorking experience in NMS/EMS based Softwares.\nExposure to Microservice Architecture based platforms and REST based APIs.\nUnderstanding of Protocols and Infrastructure in Packet (Layer2) Domain i.e MPLS, G.8032, QinQ\nExposure to Elastic Search and Cassandra databases\nExposure to Apache Kafka stream processing platform"
