   "FIELD1": 313,
   "Job Title": "Java Developer",
   "Job Description": "Who We Are:\n\nBandwidth lives for innovation! Our technology powers brands like Google, Microsoft, GoDaddy, Arlo, Netgear, Zoom, Rover and more of the most exciting leaders in technology. Our intelligent voice, messaging, 9-1-1 access, and phone number services— all backed by Bandwidth's own nationwide, all-IP voice network—allow us to power the way people communicate, connect, and do business.\n\nAt Bandwidth, your music matters when you are part of the BAND. We celebrate differences and encourage BANDmates to be their authentic selves. #jointheband\n\nWhat we are looking for:\n\nWe are looking for a passionate and talented Sr. Salesforce Developer to join our growing team and help take our Salesforce platform to the next level. You will be given a high level of responsibility for the freedom and the potential to make an immediate impact. We're seeking somebody who is a maker, a hacker, and a software craftsman. If your idea of fun is losing track of time while geeking out lighting or apex, we'd like to talk to you.\n\nWhat You'll Do:\n\nYou're gonna write great code and lots of it. You'll be a senior member of an agile software development team, and a leading voice in your team's design and implementation efforts. You'll communicate with peers to build and refactor code that is both readable and reliable due to its inherent lack of complexity. You'll also look critically at what we're building and how we're building it, and you'll originate ideas and activities that advance our craft.\n\nWhat You'll Need:\n\nIf you're our person, you probably look like this:\n\nYou have 5+ years of experience developing directly in the Salesforce platform\nYou have experience building custom Salesforce solutions utilizing lightning web components and apex for complex business processes\nYou have Salesforce Platform Developer and Platform App Builder certifications\nYou have the ability to evaluate complex business problems and turn them into solutions\nYou have experience with other technologies just as Java, Javascript, and jQuery\nYou have experience developing solutions on Sales Cloud, Service Cloud, and Heroku\nYou have experience testing and troubleshooting customizations, determining root causes\nYou have the ability to document and chart customizations in a manner that makes sense to both end-users and peers.\nYou're passionate about the craft of software engineering\n\nExtra Credit for You:\n\nWow, it'd be really great if also:\n\nYou have experience working in International Salesforce instances and understand their associated complexities\nYou have experience with Mulesoft\nYou have experience developing on other platforms such as NetSuite, Workday, or Zendesk\nYou've been a part of or led teams in an agile environment and are steeped in the methods of Scrum and Kanban\nThe Whole Person Promise:\n\nWe make a \"Whole Person\" promise to our team. You can have both meaningful work PLUS a full life at Bandwidth. We focus on accomplishing our mission as \"whole people.\" That means we take care of our people—in body, mind, and spirit.\n\nHealth: We pay 100% for benefits coverage including Medical, Dental, Vision, Prescription, Life, and Disability. Corporate chaplains, EAP and 401K match.\nFitness: 90-minute fitness lunch with a paid gym membership with shuttle service available for workouts. On-site cardio gym, locker room/showers, classes, and sponsored sports and leagues. Nutritionist and personal trainer on-site.\nVolunteer: We have a program dedicated to providing volunteer opportunities to employees, Bandwidthcares.\n\nEmployee and Applicant Privacy Notice"
