   "Job Description": "17791 DevOps Engineer II (Open)\n\nPosition Type:\n\nFull time\n\nLocation(s):\n\nIN.Bangalore.Office1\n\nPosition Details:\n\nOverview\nThis job is responsible/accountable for streamlining offerings to CSGs end customers.\nThey take solutions from development and ensure they are operationally sound prior to rolling into production.\nProducts are evaluated and prepared for installation, configuration, monitoring, diagnostics, and process / procedure to ensure minimal impact as they are released.\nProduction optimization from a personnel perspective is a critical point and leveraging technology to ensure solutions adhere to customers SLA requirements for availability.\nJob Description:\nThe incumbent is responsible for providing key support for their focused product / solution area to internal and external resources.\nSupport and maintenance of the customers production and non-production environments - including on-call support / work variety of shifts to include weekends, holidays or extra shifts/extended shifts or as needed.\nWork with L1/L2/L3/L4 support and operations teams to ensure successful deployment and operation of their application and ongoing operational activities\nIndependently building and testing reliable and well-tested solutions and once released troubleshoot any issues, actively seeking out problems and solving them.\nSupport the build and deployment infrastructure used by our delivery teams\nRespond to high severity production issues escalated by our operations teams along with root cause analysis\nTest driven development, Agile development, continuous integration, continuous deployment, DevOps automation\nCreate seamless/automated build scripts used for release management across all environments.\nContribute to the DevOps community by way of good & best practices and support mentoring/coaching and training the wider team\nComprehend customers security and data policies and ensure adherence\nLiason with cross functional teams to investigate customer issues and drive early resolution.\nPrepare, validate and Share the data which are required to cleanup/correct/reconcile as a part of fix\nExperience\n3-5 years of related experience in Technical Analyst or equivalent role or 2-3 years in computer engineering or equivalent role\nSome experience with a broad range of IT technologies: Network, Storage, Virtualization, Compute, Database, Automation, SDLC, and distributed transactions in high volume managed services or billing services provider environments\nAdditional Job Description\nUnder limited supervision, performs installations, configurations, and upgrades to CSG products.\nHands on experience in either 2 of the languages Python, C# and Shell/Powershell . Expertise in\none of this is mandatory\nOS experience Windows and Linux\nExperience in using monitoring tools\nBasic understanding and working knowledge of CI/CD tools like Chef, Jenkins etc\nAbility to troubleshoot issues and provide solution\nValidation of installation and configuration processes and procedures.\nActive participation/internship with the other teams involved in delivery (Development & Project Management).\nTroubleshooting and bug fixing for solutions once in place.\nParticipate in the on-call rotation under the supervision of a senior team member\nReleases & Promotions:\nUnder limited supervision, support the development team in releases and promotions (including core upgrades) from development through to production, as defined by Best Practices.\nValidation of release and promotion processes and procedures.\nTroubleshooting and bug fixing for solutions once in place.\nBackups & Recovery:\nWith limited supervision, establishes and maintains system and database backup and recovery policies and procedures.\nSolution & New Product Evaluation:\nAssists in the identification and analysis of the internal/external clients technical requirements.\nUnder limited supervision, gathers information from customers on technical requirements.\nUnder limited supervision, provides technical input and consultation for application deployment.\nThird Party & Open Source:\nUnder limited supervision, performs installation, configuration, and upgrades to any supporting\nthird-party software used in supporting CSG products.\nActive research and sandbox trials of open source solutions.\nExecute third party/open source compilation for requisite software.\nPull source and monitor version modifications in association with key software.\nFamiliarization of key third party products /open source projects leveraged by CSG solutions.\nCommunication & Documentation:\nEffectively communicates with customers and colleagues alike.\nProduces and maintains documentation on projects and research as assigned.\nCreates wiki documentation for solution delivery and support, as well as, automation efforts.\nResponsibility\n\n% of Time\nAdministration of infrastructure systems (upgrade, maintain, troubleshoot) such as BigIP, CVP framework, BladeLogic, Automation, ADDM, CSP/IPF 20%\nServes as subject matter expert for matters relating to system and application architecture 20%\n3rd tier support for operational production issues 40%\nParticipates in process improvement efforts within the larger technology organization 20%\nRegular and reliable attendance is required.\nOngoing\nIncumbent is accountable for professional working behavior to include; building and maintaining constructive working relationships, implementing proactive and concise communication, acting as a resource to colleagues, and engaging in collaborative thinking and problem solving while demonstrating CSGs core competencies and values.\nTypical Interactions/Relationships\nInternal Some contact with developers, dbas, operations, Systems Administrators, Global Platform Architecture.\nKnowledge, Skills and Abilities\nFamiliarity with practical agile development methodologies.\nFamiliarity with required coding (C #) and scripting languages (Shell Scripting).\nGeneral knowledge of database architecture and function.\nDemonstrates a great deal of self-drive and initiative in a highly independent environment.\nKnowledge of programming and systems analysis procedures.\nStrong oral and written/editing skills.\nGood interpersonal skills.\nKnowledge of Linux Shell and Windows PowerShell scripting.\nWorks with some independence, yet most feature level work assigned by lead. Knows when to\nseek guidance from teammates or lead.\nBalances task load to deliver in a timely manner.\nInvolved in story creation and iterative planning.\nDemonstrates solid skill and is working to gain additional experience\n3-5 years of experience in application deployment and support.\nGood Understanding of OS, Network, Database and application monitoring tools.\nDemonstrates creativity when researching or solving a situation.\nKnowledge of systems security and PCI compliance.\nBachelors Degree or equivalent experience.\nShould have worked on Agile projects and should understand\nC#\nPowerShell/ Shell Scripting\nDatabase Knowledge\nPython or pearl will be added advantage"
