   "Job Title": "Java Developer",
   "Job Description": "_Do you work hard and take pride in what you do?_\n\n_Are you optimistic and enthusiastic? Do others enjoy working with you? _\n\n_Do you treat people with kindness and respect?_\n\n_Are you curious, open-minded and committed to continuous improvement?_\nYou may be the confident and collaborative web developer we are looking for to join our technology team in Wilmington, NC!*\nAbout Queensboro: A Great Place to work!*\n· Queensboro provides customized apparel to help people share who they are with the world!\n\n· We have been in business for 38 years and continue to grow! We are well established, yet innovative & agile.\n\n· We are driven forward by 3 key values:\nAlways do the right thing\nValue relationships above all\nInnovate and have fun!\n· Please check out our *_Culture pages_ *on * _Queensboro.com_* to learn more about our team, culture and values.\n\n· We offer competitive pay, health, dental, vision, 401k, paid time off, and a great employee purchase program.\n\n· We care about our employees, community and customers.\n\n· We encourage fresh ideas, new technologies & continuous improvement.\n\n· We thrive in a casual, friendly & professional environment, love to have fun and promote growth and happiness.\n\n· We’re passionate about what we do, and our diverse and unique office is filled with some of the greatest minds in the business.\nAbout Being a Queensboro Developer*\n· Our technology team is small, friendly, and always looking for ways to improve.\n\n· As a developer you will:\nParticipate, start-to-finish, on a wide variety of challenging projects.\nContribute to all aspects of software development including the design, architecture, development, documentation, and testing of our system.\nDevelop code for internal systems and our customer-facing websites.\nContribute to new system development, while also participating in the maintenance and conversion of our existing codebases.\nCollaborate and communicate with technical and non-technical personnel.\nWork as part of an established, yet innovative and growing e-Commerce company\n· We understand the importance of work/life balance and enjoy a positive, fun environment with a casual dress code and minimal meetings for developers.\nJob Duties: Necessary Requirements, Skills, and Qualifications*\n· Experience building database-driven PHP applications is a must.\n\n· Any additional experience with the following: Laravel, MySQL, Postgres, JavaScript, JQuery, VueJS, Bootstrap, HTML, CSS, Amazon Web Services (EC2, S3, SES, SNS, RDS, Elasticache, etc.)\n\n· *\\*\\*\\*This position requires your presence in our Wilmington, NC office.\\*\\*\\** (Sorry, no H1B Visa sponsorships will be considered.)\n\n· Bachelor’s degree in computer science is preferred\n\nJob Type: Full-time\n\nPay: $65,000.00 - $100,000.00 per year\n\nBenefits:\n401(k)\n401(k) matching\nDental insurance\nDisability insurance\nEmployee assistance program\nEmployee discount\nFlexible schedule\nHealth insurance\nLife insurance\nPaid time off\nVision insurance\nSchedule:\n8 hour shift\nMonday to Friday\nEducation:\nBachelor's (Required)\nLocation:\nWilmington, NC 28401 (Required)\nWork authorization:\nUnited States (Required)\nWork Location:\nOne location\nThis Company Describes Its Culture as:\nInnovative -- innovative and risk-taking\nPeople-oriented -- supportive and fairness-focused\nTeam-oriented -- cooperative and collaborative\nCompany's website:\nqueensboro.com\nBenefit Conditions:\nWaiting period may apply\nOnly full-time employees eligible\nWork Remotely:\nNo"
