   "Job Title": "Network Administrator",
   "Job Description": "Is managing large networks and building data centers your cup of tea? Then you will thrive and grow with our IT team. We are looking for IT rock stars with a zeal to become IT managers and Senior consultants. You will build new IT infrastructure from the bottom up.\nResponsibilities\nWindows and Linux systems, business applications, anti-virus protection, email and authentication administration.\nPerform software and application development, installation, and upgrades.\nPlan and implement network security, including building Firewalls, managing host security, file permissions, backup and disaster recovery plans, file system integrity, and adding and deleting users.\nEvaluate and/or recommend purchases of computers, network hardware, peripheral equipment, and software.\nInstall, configure, and maintain workstations, file Servers, Ethernet networks, network cabling, and other related equipment, devices, and systems; adds or upgrades and configures modems, disk drives, data acquisition boards, CD ROM units, printers, and related equipment.\nTroubleshoot networks, systems, and applications to identify and correct malfunctions and other operational difficulties.\nNetwork administration (including backup, security management, user account management, e-mail systems including e-mail web server, Internet access, office systems and applications support).\nSupports server, network and desktop hardware, software and applications.\nPlans, implements, and supports the network and computing infrastructure plan.\nManages small to medium sized projects according to agreed upon budgets and schedules.\nNetwork Infrastructure design and troubleshooting; WAN and TCP/IP administration; Software/Hardware, testing, maintenance, support; and advanced end-user support.\nAbility to identify and resolve computer system malfunctions and operational problems.\nAbility to provide technical training to end users and learn and support new systems and applications.\n\nPlatforms/Applications\nLinux, ClearOS, Windows Server 200x, Windows XP to 7, VMWare, MS Office, MS Exchange, Tally , PeopleSoft or any ERP system, LAN/WAN, WMS systems, Microsoft SQL support\nMinimum Qualifications\n2 year Associate’s Degree\n4+ years experience PC and network support experience in a Unix/Microsoft environment.\nComputing and network hardware and peripheral equipment.\nKnowledge of computer and/or network security systems, applications, procedures, and techniques.\nWindows Servers and desktop products.\nDemonstrated ability to administer a 250+ node network including Firewalls.\nDemonstrated ability to support networked printers and photocopiers.\nPreferred Qualifications\nAny Graduate with completion of echnical courses like GNIIT (which involves more than 1 years of technical training), MCSC,/MCSE, MCP, Red Hat Certified RHCE, VCP etc.\nExperience with ClearOS, SAN/NAS.\nExperience with Cloud based networks.\nMinimum 2 years experience as Windows Systems Administrator\nMinimum 2 years experience as a Linux Systems Administrator\nSupervising or training juniors, and being the consultant for computer problems beyond the knowledge of technical support staff."
