   "Job Title": "Software Engineer",
   "Job Description": "Job title: Software\nEngineer\n\nThe department is part of the CONTROLLING AND FINANCE global team with\nthe main focus to optimize business processes using standard process and use IT\nas key tools to add value to the organization.\n\nThe aim is to increase efficiency in the financial reporting processes\nand applications for Siemens which operates the world over. Clients/Business\nPartners are global Head Quarter Functions in Germany as well as similar\nfunctions which operate throughout the worldwide organization.\n\nThis is\nyour role. What part will you play?\nPerform as a self-motivated software engineer,\ndesigning and implementing portions of a next-generation enterprise\nproduct.\nCreate eminently high quality, testable units\nof code. Create and execute unit tests and contribute to integration test\nplanning.\nFocus on delivering working results meeting\nthe given functional requirements and quality attributes.\nStrong software development skills and\nfamiliarity with current industry best practices.\nFlexible working as a contributing member of a\nsmall collaborative team.\nStrong problem-solving skills.\nStrong organizational and communication\nskills.\nAbility to travel to domestic and\ninternational locations.\nUse your\nskills to move the world forward.\nExperience with web programming and respective\nframeworks (JavaScript, Node.js, React, React Native, CSS, Python).\nExperience with containers and orchestration\ntechnologies (Docker, Kubernetes).\nExperience with deployment on cloud platforms\n(AWS, AZURE)\nExperience with API standards (REST, JSON,\nXML).\nExperience with modern software engineering\nmethods and the respective tooling (e.g. Git)\nThis role\nis based in Kalwa - Mumbai, where you’ll get the chance to work with teams\nimpacting entire cities, countries – and the shape of things to come.\n\nWe’re\nSiemens. A collection of over 379,000 minds building the future, one day at a\ntime in over 200 countries. We're dedicated to equality, and we encourage\napplications that reflect the diversity of the communities we work in. All\nemployment decisions at Siemens are based on qualifications, merit and business\nneed. Bring your curiosity and inventiveness, and help us shape tomorrow.\n\nWe are\ncommitted to be an equal opportunity employer open to all irrespective of\ngender, sexual orientation, caste, region, religion, political ideologies,\nabilities, etc.\n\nOrganization: Controlling and Finance\n\nCompany: Siemens Technology and Services Private Limited\n\nExperience Level: Early Professional\n\nJob Type: Full-time"
