   "Job Title": "Software Engineer",
   "Job Description": "Ellie Mae is the leading cloud-based platform provider for the mortgage finance industry. Ellie Mae’s technology solutions enable lenders to originate more loans, reduce origination costs, and reduce the time to close, all while ensuring the highest levels of compliance, quality and efficiency. Visit ‪ EllieMae.com to learn more.\n\nDuties & Responsibilities\n\nQualification & Requirements\nDevelop Product components & modules.\nDesign, build, and maintain efficient, reusable, and reliable C++ code\nImplement performance and quality modules\nIdentify bottlenecks and bugs, and devise solutions to these problems\nHelp maintain code quality, organization, and automatization\nPerform peer code review of components & modules.\nAssist in developing solution prototypes and technology evaluation\nAcquire deeper knowledge of Technologies used in the Product.\nResolve integration/certification/production issues by collaborating with other teams\nIdentify areas of improvement in module development.\nSupport Operations on-site or off-site in monitoring production, to resolve production issues and developing tools\nAssist in training & mentoring new team members through the “buddy” program (basic training only)\nDegree in Computer Science or equivalent\n3+ years experience as a software engineer or equivalent\nProficient in C or C++ and demonstrate good coding practices\nGood knowledge of data structures and algorithms\nThorough knowledge of the standard library, STL containers\nFamiliarity with templating in C++\nKnowledge of the latest C++11 standard is appreciated\nExposure to product development\nKnowledge of image processing is an advantage\nProficient understanding of code versioning tools, such as Git\nExposure to Test Driven Development is good to have\nExposure to Test Driven Development is good to have\nEllie Mae is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. Women, minorities, people with disabilities, and veterans are encouraged to apply.\n\nWe do not accept resumes from headhunters, placement agencies, or other suppliers that have not signed a formal agreement with us."
