   "Job Title": "JavaScript Developer",
   "Job Description": "We are looking for a great JavaScript developer who is proficient with React.js. Your primary focus will be on developing user interface components and implementing them following well-known React.js workflows (such as Flux or Redux). You will ensure that these components and the overall application are robust and easy to maintain. You will coordinate with the rest of the team working on different layers of the infrastructure. Therefore, a commitment to collaborative problem solving, sophisticated design, and quality products are important.\nClient Basically Looking For Skills To Be Present In Candidate:\na. Looking for great java script developer with React.js\nb. Well know react.js workflow (Redux or Flux)\nc. Commitment to a collaborative problem solving, sophisticated design, and quality product are important.\nMandatory Skills:\ni. Java script, Dom Manipulation (Document Object Model an application programming interface API), JavaScript object model (Document Modification and accessing)\nii. Expertise Babel (Translator for JavaScript) and Web Pack (mega multi translator that woks with all kinds of languages (or assets)\niii. Understanding React.js (open source java script) and core competencies (HTML + CSS, JSX, JavaScript Fundamentals + ES6, GIT, Node + NPM – Node Package Manager, or Redux)\niv. Experience with popular React.js workflow (such as Flux – Multiple stores per app and Redux – Single Store App)\nv. Newer Specification of ECMA Script (European Computer Manufacturer’s Association – Standard for scripting languages such as JavaScript, Jscript etc.)\nvi. Experience with DSL (Domain Specific Language – Small expressive programming language custom designed for specific task) immutable.js\nvii. Knowledge of Isomorphic [Server that renders the initial HTML for the client using React components and React.renderToString ()] / Universal React (which will be used on any environment which isn’t undefined (i.e. not local) is must.\nviii. Familiarity with Restful API (To take advantage of existing protocol)\nix. Knowledge of modern authorization mechanism such as JSON Web Token (Java Script Object Notation – Authentication Mechanism)\nx. Familiarity of Modern Frontend Build Pipelines and tools\na. NPM (Package Manager)\nb. YARN (Package Manager)\nc. GRUNT (Task Runner)\nd. Gulp (Task Runner)\ne. BROWSERIFY (Module Loader/ Bundler)\nf. WEBPACK (Module Loader/ Bundler)\nXii. Understand business requirement and translate them into technical requirement.\nXiii. A knack of Benchmarking (Evaluating) and Optimization (Process, or methodology of making something)\nXiv. Familiarity with code versioning tools such as GIT (Global Information Tracker) and mercurial.\nXvi. Experience with SASS (short for syntactically awesome style sheet), CSS Next (Cascading Style Sheet), and LESS (Learner Style Sheets)\nXvii. Experience with React Native (Open source mobile application framework; used for developing applications for Android, Android TV, IOS, MACOS, TVOS, Web, Windows and UWP (Universal Window Platform) is plus.\nª Should have great debugging skills and can optimize code with Profiling and Heap memory management (this skill will be used as one of the most deciding factors for selecting the candidate).\nª Important Skills:\nª Proficient Communication in English is must.\nª Experience in dealing with client directly.\nª Managed the team of at least 20+ developers.\nª Open to work in a startup.\nSpecialty: PHP Hypertext Processor (earlier called Personal Home Page), Backbone JS, Angular JS, Node JS, Zend Framework, Apigility, Symphony Framework 2, React JS, Progressive Web Application, PWA (Progressive Web Application)\nLocation: Gujarat/Baroda/Mumbai/Pune/Vadodra (WHF: Applicable for lifetime).\nApplication Deadline: 30/12/2020\nJob Type: Full-time\nSalary: Up to ₹2,000,000.00 per year\nSchedule:\nFlexible shift\nExperience:\nwork: 8 years (Preferred)\ntotal work: 8 years (Required)\nJavaScript: 5 years (Preferred)\nEducation:\nBachelor's (Preferred)\nWork Remotely:\nTemporarily due to COVID-19"
