   "Job Title": "Java Developer",
   "Job Description": "Key Components to the Role: *\n• Manager / Lead Developer (Hands-on Development)\n\n• C# / VB.NET experience is a must (Minimum 8 years)\n\n• ASP.NET / ASP.NET Core experience is a must (Minimum 8 years)\n\n• Web API experience is a must (Minimum 8 years)\n\n• MS-SQL experience is a must (Minimum 8 years)\n\n• Familiarity with Object Oriented design concepts, data structures and algorithms\n\n• Some experience in web applications / services\n\n• Prior experience in managing a team of 5+ developers\nPosition Summary: *\nMicrologic Associates is seeking an experienced, hands-on Software Development Manager to lead a team of developers and to help refine operational procedures within the department. At Micrologic, our software technology products are an integral part of our services & success.\n\nDevelopment responsibilities will include working on new system features as well as maintaining and supporting existing applications. Additionally, the Software Development Manager will assist in developing and implementing the technical strategy, development methodology, and necessary IT operational procedures to sustain a reliable set of production systems.\n\nAs a team leader within the Development team, this position will be responsible for the planning and delivery of appropriate solutions to meet required specifications and timelines and will work closely with other departments to ensure products and services meet all technical, functional, and performance related requirements.\n\nThe Software Development Manager should be a self-starter, have a can-do attitude, and possess a strong development background. This position has a strong team emphasis and will require exceptional relationship building skills with the ability to create effective partnerships with business, shared services, and other IT Support areas. This position will report to our Director of Development Services.\nResponsibilities: *\n• Monitor systems and applications uptime and performance with a goal of minimizing downtime\n\n• Monitor system deployment and maintenance for impacts to production support\n\n• Support and maintain production environments and applications\n\n• Assist in developing the technology strategy for the organization; research and implement technical tools needed to optimize the business processes and workflows\n\n• Review requirements and determine technical design and implementation alternatives\n\n• Responsible for department’s technologies including JIRA, CRM and ticketing system\n\n• Implement development guidelines and processes including coding standards, documentation and audit trail, code maintenance, peer reviews and check-in/checkout procedures\n\n• Mentor, coach and provide technical guidance ensuring team is successful to deliver quality products\n\n• Ability to work in a fast-paced environment, recognize and react to changing business needs and effectively prioritize tasks\n\n• Ability to meet deadlines, identify issues and resolve with minimal direction\nRequirements: *\n• 8-10 years of progressive broad-based information systems experience\n\n• 5+ years of management/supervisory experience in application implementation and production support\n\n• Experience working in SQL Server environments with strong SQL Server development skills\n\n• Hands-on experience with many disparate technologies, ranging from front-end user interfaces through to back-end system\n\n• Strong technical skills with demonstrated experience in SQL, C#, .NET\n\n• Prior use of software tools to prototype data structures, process, and system functionality\n(screens, reports, audit logs), data validation and storage logic\n\n• Capable of providing time estimates and preparing design documents, developing, coding, and testing\n\n• Experience with (SDLC) software methodologies such as Scrum/Agile, certification a plus\n\n• Good understanding of Project Management Principles, certification preferred\n\n• Strong analytical and troubleshooting skills\n\n• Ability to multi-task and manage shifting priorities in a fast-paced environment\n\n• Drawn to both strategize and execute; moreover, able to do so successfully in a fast-paced environment.\n\n• Superior written and verbal communication skills\n\n• Skilled at coaching, developing, and managing early-career and more seasoned professionals\n\n\\* Must live in New Jersey or near by\n\nJob Type: Full-time\n\nPay: $110,000.00 - $125,000.00 per year\n\nBenefits:\n401(k)\n401(k) Matching\nDental Insurance\nHealth Insurance\nLife Insurance\nPaid Time Off\nReferral Program\nVision Insurance\nSchedule:\nMonday to Friday\nExperience:\nprogressive broad-based information systems: 8 years (Preferred)\nLocation:\nTownship of Roxbury, NJ (Required)\nWork authorization:\nUnited States (Required)\nWork Location:\nOne location\nCompany's website:\nhttp://micrologic.net/\nBenefit Conditions:\nWaiting period may apply\nWork Remotely:\nNo"
