   "Job Title": "Wordpress Developer",
   "Job Description": "UWorld is a worldwide leader in online test prep for college entrance, undergraduate, graduate, and professional licensing exams throughout the United States. Since 2003, over million students have trusted us to help them prepare for high-stakes examinations.\nWe are seeking a WordPress Specialist who enjoys taking on new challenges and is passionate about designing and building attractive and functional websites that meet the specifications of our end-users and stakeholders. The WordPress Specialist will be responsible for UI design and front-end development, being mindful of user experience and site integration as it pertains to our various Test Prep products.\nYour Role\n• Meeting with stakeholders to conceptualize their ideas and discuss website design and function\n• Designing and building the website front-end and implementing new features and functionality\n• Converting comprehensive layout and wireframes into working HTML pages\n• Conducting website performance tests across all devices and monitoring the performance of the live website\n• Troubleshooting content issues\n• Conducting WordPress training with stakeholders\n• Ensuring high-performance and availability, and managing the technical aspects of the content management system\n• Ensuring consistent style across platforms and browsers\n• Resizing and optimizing icons and media files as needed\nYour Experience\n• Degree in computer science or related field\n• 5+ year(s) of experience in developing front-end pages in Wordpress\n• Working knowledge of front-end technologies including HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap, and jQuery\n• Experience building user interfaces for websites and/or web applications\n• Experience with responsive and adaptive design\n• Ability to understand CSS changes and their ramifications to ensure consistent style across platforms and browsers\n• Ability to convert wireframes into working HTML pages\n• Knowledge of how to interact with RESTful APIs and formats (JSON, XML)\n• Proficiency in code versioning tools such as Git, VSTS, BitBucket etc.\n• Understanding of PHP back-end development\n• Comfortable with debugging tools such as Chrome Inspector and Firebug\n• Experience working in an Agile environment\n• Working knowledge of image editing software (e.g. Photoshop)\nSoft Skills\n• Proficient written and verbal communication skills (email, phone, etc.)\n• Excellent analytical, communication and research skills\n• Excellent attention to detail and organization skills and ability to articulate ideas clearly and concisely\n• Ability to work effectively within a changing environment that is going through high growth\n• Exceptional follow-through, personal drive, and ability to understand direction and feedback"
