   "Job Title": "Java Developer",
   "Job Description": "COMPANY OVERVIEW\n\nPatientTrak is a leading, cloud-based, healthcare SaaS application used by healthcare organizations to reduce wait times, build their brand, and improve patient satisfaction. Our software solutions enables leading healthcare providers across the nation to track patients, improve online reputation management, send/receive automated surveys and communicate with patients via SMS text messaging.\n\nPlease see us at: www.patienttrak.net\n\nDUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES\n\nWe are seeking an experienced, enthusiastic, full stack, software developer to support SaaS as well as custom programming for customer implementations.\n\nThis individual will be responsible for various new feature developments, implementing improvements and changes to the software application as well as troubleshooting customer issues. Scrum methodology is key to our product release cycle, so this individual will excel if they have worked on a scrum team before. The right candidate should be entrepreneurial minded and preferably has some healthcare application and HL7 experience.\n\nREQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES\nWeb Applications developer in the .NET/Visual Studio\nExperience with Microsoft SQL Server\nIIS configuration\nHTML, XML/XSL , Ajax\nJavaScript, JQuery, Bootstrap\nC#, VB.net\nTelerik Controls\nCreation of and systems integration with web services\nExperience developing and maintaining systems with 3rd party API’s\nDemonstrated knowledge of web hosting and web site management\nExperience with GIT and Software Branching\nKnowledge of tools such as Jira, TFS, or Wrike for User Story Tracking\nQUALIFICATIONS\nComfortable in a small growth company environment; flexibility and adaptability is a must.\nResults-oriented and self – disciplined.\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science or equivalent field preferred\nMinimum of 5-7 years of broad experience in programming and design\nFamiliar with estimating user stories via product backlog grooming\nWorking in a Scrum/Agile environment a plus\nEntrepreneurial mindset\nSALARY\n\nThe salary is based on the candidates experience.\n\nJob Type: Full-time\n\nCOVID-19 considerations:\nWe provide closed offices and a safe work environment. Candidates may be able to work at home depending on the project.\n\nExperience:\n.net: 5 years (Required)\nLocation:\nFranklin, WI (Required)\nWork Location:\nOne location\nVisa Sponsorship Potentially Available:\nNo: Not providing sponsorship for this job\nCompany's website:\nwww.patienttrak.net\nWork Remotely:\nTemporarily due to COVID-19"
