   "Job Title": "Django Developer",
   "Job Description": "Description\n\nAbout the position:\nDesignation: Python Lead (Python + Django)\n\nJob Location: Gurgaon\n\nReporting To: Architect\n\nVacancy: 5\n\nCab- No\nWorking Days: 5\nShift: Day shift job\n\nExperience: 5 years plus. Incumbent should have had prior experience of working on new solutions, technologies, creating architecture. Should have managed team (at least 4-5 people)\n\nKey Competencies:\n\nExpert programmer – exceptional skills in frameworks, new solutions development, system design, enhancement and modernization (Python, Django, Mysql, Front-end technologies – must haves; Redis/Memcache, Node.js - preferred)\nProven project management skills including responsibility for delivering to project timetables, and expertise in providing technical solutions.\nAbility to simultaneously work on and manage multiple tasks within the same assignment and prioritize effectively.\nStrong Architecture knowledge and skill – experience of building architecture to build systems that supports business goals. Understanding of various architectural styles.\nHighly motivated individual with ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment.\nStrong interpersonal skills and able to interact effectively within teams, external team (Marketing, Sales, Product), management and partners.\nStrong analytical ability to create innovative solutions, logical and problem-solving approach on complex issues.\nExcellent verbal/written communication skills\n\nRole/ Responsibilities:\n\nAs a Lead - Solutions you will be responsible for: Project and Release management – this will include\nmanaging end to end delivery of projects, measuring and adhering to defined TATs\nAllocation of resources and people management\nCross team collaboration (QA, Platform and Delivery) to ensure project implementation\nCreate process frameworks –\nTo install solutions by determining and designing system specifications, standards and programming\nSolutions by developing documentation, flowcharts, layouts, diagrams, charts, code comments and clear code\nTo determine operational feasibility by evaluating analysis, problem definition, requirements, solution development and proposed solutions\n\nDesigning solutions and architecture:\n\nConvert product specs to tech specs\nFeasibility analysis of products\nTrain and coach other team members"
