   "Job Title": "JavaScript Developer",
   "Job Description": "No relocation needed, can telework from home, required good Internet.*\nPlease send in your current and expected CTC too. **Please send in your current and expected CTC too.*\nWho is TEKgile?*\nWe are a tech company headquartered in Trivandrum, Kerala, that works with our international partners to deliver modern apps and software for various types of businesses. We work with global companies and various clients to always push the limits of web and server applications.\nWhy would I want to be a JavaScript Developer at TEKgile?*\nTEKgile and our International partner company aims to continue its growth trajectory in Japan and have a variety of geospatial web app projects to work on. Software and app improvements are vital to the success of the company and are looking to grow our team to add new features to what is being offered. You will be working with our Product Manager, who is based in Japan as well as our Technical manager in Trivandrum. The team focuses on all product life cycle, bugs, and features that relate to the existing clients and future needs of the project.\n\nThe JavaScript Developer role is focused on building various web app dashboards focused around geospatial data, and continuing to grow the functionality and capabilities of our frameworks. Responsibilities include helping to grow the features of existing projects and new projects. You would be partnered with other team members to assist with various DevOps tasks.\nWe are looking for someone that is: *\nLooking to take ownership of your tasks and be held accountable for their quality and completion\nInterested in modern applications\nCode ninja with an attention to detail\nBeing great at what you do and enjoy doing it\nWhat would I be doing?*\nSupport the development of server and web applications that are based on JavaScript (ExtJS 6, NodeJS).\nFocused on supporting the continued development and improvements to the existing and new JavaScript applications for frontend and backend.\nImplementing features independently or with team members\nWriting unit tests, internal and external documentation.\nDebugging, and problem-solving bugs.\nWorking with SQL based databases\nWorking in the AWS Cloud environment.\nWhat key skills and experience do I need?*\nProficiency in English\nStrong understanding of and experience in JavaScript (MVC & MVVM)\nStrong understanding of NodeJS, Express and ES6\nExperience in web app JavaScript (Bootstrap, jQuery)\nExperience in both functional and object-oriented programming\nGood understanding of SQL\nExperience in writing Unit Tests\nIt would be great if you can also bring: *\nExperience in PostgreSQL and PostGIS\nExperience in ExtJS 6.x\nExperience in HTML/CSS\nGood understanding of NoSQL (MongoDB/ElasticSearch)\nExperience in Amazon AWS Lambda, API Gateway, EC2, S3, SNS, SQS\nUnderstanding and experience in OAuth v2\nWhat are the perks?*\nMonday to Friday schedule (5 day weeks / 40 hour work weeks)\nUp to 5% performance bonus (paid quarterly)\nCompetitive salary\nPersonal laptop stipend\nAbility to work from home anywhere in India\nCompany Values*\nQuality service *- We make sure all of our customers that use our product have the best experience.\nAbility to adapt *- Being in a startup lifestyle and new technology space, we look for team members that are always willing to adapt to the constant change.\nPushing the limits *- We feel that there is always room to improve and be the best in our space. Everyone's input is valued and encouraged to make everything better.\nHelp the team *- \"How can I help?\" is a common phrase where we work. It is not only about completing your goals and tasks but important that we pitch in to help make sure the team hits their goals as well.\nJob Type: Full-time\n\nExperience:\nJS: 3 years (Preferred)\ntotal work: 4 years (Preferred)\nEducation:\nBachelor's (Preferred)\nWork Remotely:\nYes"
