   "Job Title": "JavaScript Developer",
   "Job Description": "About EdCast:\n\nEdCast is the AI-Powered Knowledge Cloud solution for unified discovery, personalized learning and knowledge management across the enterprise. Its award-winning platform is used internationally by Global 2000 companies and large government organizations, including NASSCOM and World Economic Forum, to solve the discovery and curation problems across all external and internal knowledge sources. EdCast's offerings include its Learning Experience Platform (LXP) and MyGuide's in-app guides, intelligence, and automation for business software.\n\nWebsite: www.edcast.com\n\nExternal Title: Software Engineer (JavaScript + React)\n\nLocation: Indore/Mumbai\n\nYear of Experience: 0 to 3 Years\n\nRequirements\n\nKey Result Areas include:\n\nExtensive experience in at least one modern JavaScript MV-VM/MVC frameworks like React or Angular\nHands on experience in Reactjs of minimum 1.5 yrs.\nStrong expertise with Javascript, HTML, CSS, and writing cross-browser compatible code.\nGood understanding of build tools like Grunt, Gulp and Webpack etc.\nGood understanding of JavaScript Dom manipulation Techniques.\nGood to have working experience on Redux, Sagas and Thunk etc. along with React.\nFamiliarity with testing frameworks (Ex. Jasmine) and test runners (Ex. Karma)\nShould have debugging and problem-solving skills\nGood time-management skills and a good team player\n\nDuties & Responsibilities:\n\nDevelop user interfaces with the latest frontend technologies\nResearch, analyze, and develop product features of increasingly complex nature.\nMake design and technical decisions.\nEnsure high performance of all systems developed\n\nWhat you would need:\n\nGraduate / Post- Graduate (Any) (Preferably from Technical Background) from a premier college a must\nExcellent communication.\n\nSkills OR Traits: (Top 5 skill sets is mandatory)\n\nStrong programming and problem solving skills\nStrong proficiency in react\nStrong proficiency in javascript, html and css\nGood knowledge of RESTful API and Microservices\n\nBenefits\n\nAn opportunity to get ahead in your career by building a great and exciting portfolio that helps others get ahead in theirs. You will be joining a truly passionate and multicultural team willing to make a difference and positively disrupt the way learning is done within organizations.\n\nWe believe in lifelong learning. We believe we can create abundant opportunities for workforce learning and up-skilling within the organization ecosystems. We have the spark, the ambition, the drive and the passion of making an impact in the world."
