   "FIELD1": 1757,
   "Job Title": "Wordpress Developer",
   "Job Description": "WordPress Support Engineer\n\n\nAcquia is the open digital experience company. We provide the world's most ambitious brands with products built around Drupal to allow them to embrace innovation and create customer moments that matter. At Acquia, we believe in the power of community and collaboration — giving our customers and partners the freedom to build tomorrow on their terms.\n\nHeadquartered in the U.S., we have been named one of North America's fastest growing software companies by Deloitte and Inc. Magazine, rated a leader by the analyst community, named one of the Best Places to Work in India by Great Place to Work. We are Acquia. We are building for the future and we want you to be a part of it!\n\nSummary:\n\nYou get to guide and drive technical application design for one of Acquia's most tenured clients. This client has a sophisticated Wordpress footprint and requires a support engineer to assist in their continued success.\n\nJob Requirements:\n\n\nIn this role your expertise and craftsmanship will shape the next generation of leveraged site management and managed hosting of a Wordpress application. If you are interested in microservices architecture and are compelled to evolve to the next level on a product that is critical to Acquia's success, this is your opportunity!\n\nBasic Qualifications:\nDetailed knowledge of WordPress, PHP and MySQL (this is not an entry-level position)\nStrong JavaScript, HTML and CSS skills\nExperienced in troubleshooting and supporting sophisticated WordPress sites\nKnowledge of hosting environments, domains and DNS\nComfortable with working in a fast-paced, technical support environment\nHave a positive demeanor and are comfortable working independently and as a member of a hardworking team\nHave outstanding written and verbal communication skills\nPassion for the web, open source development, and overall client success\nStrong problem-solving abilities, initiative, and are comfortable performing under pressure\nGood knowledge of WordPress security features, plug-ins and know-how to secure WordPress Enterprise sites.\nExtra credit:\n\nSkillset of orchestration technologies such as Kubernetes\nKnowledge of configuration management tools such as Ansible\nExperience with containerization technologies such as Docker\nKnowledge of or experience with other CMS technologies and/or open-source technologies\nCrafting and implementing microservices\nComfortable with large scale task automation\nCloud hosting experience (e.g., Amazon Web Services, Google Compute, Azure)\nIndividuals seeking employment at Acquia are considered without regard to race, color, religion, caste, creed, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, gender identity, or sexual orientation. Whatever you answer will not be considered in the hiring process or thereafter."
