   "Job Title": "DevOps Engineer",
   "Job Description": "We're ADVANCED\n\nWe’re one of the UK’s largest and fastest growing software companies. True partnership is the defining thing that enables us to stand out from the competition. We pride ourselves on delivering focused software solutions for the public sector, enterprise commercial and health & care organizations that simplify complex business challenges and deliver immediate and high-quality value.\n\nPOST TITLE: DevOps Engineer\n\nLOCATION: Bangalore - India\n\nREPORTING TO: Respective Line Manager\n\nEXPERIENCE LEVEL: 3-6 Years\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION:\n\nExciting opportunity to join the DevOps Centre Of Excellence as a DevOps Engineer.\n\nThe successful candidate will work with teams across the business. Working with multiple technology stacks in a wide variety of environments. The role will involve:\n\no Creating and enhancing automation (CI/CD)\n\no Expanding the toolchain functionality and availability, including adding integration points to the toolchain API\n\no Working with teams to improve processes\n\no Defining and delivering key development and operational patterns and practices.\n\nThe candidate will need to have a positive attitude and a strong desire to learn. The team works very closely together and the candidate will need to be a strong fit able to work with all team members as well as independently.\n\nKey to success in the role is:\n\no Able self manage multiple concurrent small projects, including managing priorities between projects\n\no Strong problem solving\n\no Able to quickly learn and on-board new technologies\n\no Strong communication and documentation skills\n\nThe successful candidate will work with the following key technologies and should be skilled in at least 2 of the following, with knowledge of at least 4\n\no Jenkins Build Pipelines (Groovy)\n\no Node.js\n\no AWS CloudFormation\n\no PowerShell\n\no Bash\n\no Docker\n\no AWS Services (EC2, ECS, S3, IAM, SNS, SQS, Lambda, API Gateway)"
