   "Job Title": "Wordpress Developer",
   "Job Description": "Corporate Overview\n\nFounded in 2005, DCKAP is on the path to creating a global digital commerce community for brands and companies in the commerce space. Entrepreneurship is in our DNA and it fuels our innovations helping us develop products and solutions. DCKAP is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive organisational culture.\n\nDCKAP provides Digital Commerce Products and Solutions for organisations of all sizes to make the merchant’s life easier. Our platform includes Cloras, Productimize, flexiPIM, VizB and QA Touch. Our cloud-based product suite is widely used by 100+ businesses globally.\n\nWe are headquartered in Austin, TX with an office in Chennai, TN, India.\n\nWhy work at DCKAP?\n\nAt DCKAP you will have the opportunity to be part of a highly active ecosystem which is transforming the way the world looks at eCommerce. You will be responsible for both back-end and front-end development, including creating WordPress themes and plugins.\n\nPrimary Job Responsibilities:\n\nHands-on software development skills, deep technical expertise across the entire software delivery process.\nYou will work closely with the Marketing team to write well documented code, design, implement and manage the WordPress websites.\n\nJob Requirements:\n\nExcellent knowledge of WordPress, PHP, MySQL, CSS, HTML and jQuery.\nExperience creating custom WordPress CMS websites and plugins using the best practice.\nTheme/template integration and creation of custom post types.\nExperience working on any one of the page builders is an added advantage.\nStrong understanding of latest industry trends and content management systems.\nExperience using SVN software and GIT.\nGood organisational skills with the ability to track and prioritise numerous tasks.\nProactive personality with a proven track record of following through and delivering on responsibilities.\nHighly adaptive and capable of being an individual contributor and working as part of a team.\n\nAlone we can do so little. TOGETHER we can aim for the sky\n\nDCKAP is an equal opportunity employer. As a diversified company, we’re trying to address the gender dominated workforce. 50% of our employees are women starting from a beginner to a leadership role. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, national origin, pregnancy status, sex, age, marital status, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other characteristics protected by applicable laws, regulations and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment."
