   "Job Description": "We are a growing software engineering company based in Medford, Oregon that offers its employees a positive team environment, opportunities for growth and skill building, and management invested in your success.\nThe Company: *Vesigo Studios pursues continuous innovation in software development. Our expertise over the past 20 years has ensured customer confidence in our product. We provide a busy, yet low-stress team environment with room for growth, and are known for the great care we take with clients and employees alike.\nOur management seeks to fit each employee into a position that uniquely highlights their best qualities and skills.\nWe believe that quality customer service is the cornerstone of our success.\nThe Position: * We're looking for an energetic, self-motivated software developer to join our development team. Responsibilities include developing web-based, desktop, cloud, and API applications using C#, Visual Basic .NET, and the .NET Framework. The applicant will meet regularly with company management and senior developers to discuss project specifications and their implementation. In turn, the applicant will develop components to that specification.\nThe developer is responsible for full lifecycle development including requirement analysis, coding, unit testing, and documentation. The developer should have a strong working knowledge of the internet and good working experience with SQL and relational databases.\n\nThe developer works to understand business requirements and objectives and collaborates with the senior architect to outline technical solutions. The developer may work with a team or independently within a project domain and is responsible for delivering all functionality within an application module. In other words, a full-stack developer is required.\nRequirements: *\nComfortable acting as a full-stack developer\nSolid experience in Microsoft .NET languages, including C# and Visual Basic .NET (mandatory)\nSolid knowledge of object-oriented concepts\nSolid understanding of ASP.Net, HTML, CSS, and JavaScript\nAbility to analyze and troubleshoot existing program code to isolate and correct issues\nAbility to work as part of a team with specific direction, or as an individual project lead with only high-level direction\nCritical thinking and problem solving skills\nUnderstand the use of industry tools and technology and how the implementation of these affect project goals\nAttention to detail\nStrong written and verbal communication skills\nAbility to create technical documentation for internal and external users that accurately describes the configuration of technology utilized to implement a development solution\nAbility to meet deadlines and hold oneself accountable\nAbove all, we are looking for exceptionally smart, professionally motivated, and driven people who can join our team and contribute for years to come. Apply if you feel you are ready to elevate your experience through exposure to multiple projects across various applications.\nCompensation: *\nHours of operation are Monday through Friday, 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM\nThe pay range is $33k-$60k per year, with the opportunity for raises depending on proficiency in solving software and technical issues\nWe offer paid vacation and holidays, health/dental/vision insurance plans, along with 100% coverage of direct primary healthcare\nWe offer a comfortable office with a fully stocked snack and drink area\nWhy Should You Apply?*\nSteady, reasonable hours\nOpportunities for on-the-job training and advancement\nManagement invested in your success\nLow-stress and positive team environment\n_Please reply with a copy of your resume and the answers to these questions: _*\nWhich of the required job skills do you feel you are strongest at?\nWhich part of this job description do you think will be most challenging?\nWhat part of this project most appeals to you?\nDo you have any questions about the job description?\nJob Type: Full-time\n\nPay: $33,000.00 - $60,000.00 per year\n\nBenefits:\nDental insurance\nHealth insurance\nPaid time off\nVision insurance\nSchedule:\n8 hour shift\nMonday to Friday\nAbility to Commute/Relocate:\nMedford, OR 97504 (Required)\nEducation:\nAssociate (Required)\nExperience:\n.NET: 3 years (Preferred)\nC#: 3 years (Preferred)\nVisual Basic: 3 years (Preferred)\nWeb development: 3 years (Preferred)\nWork Location:\nOne location\nCompany's website:\nhttps://www.vesigo.com\nBenefit Conditions:\nWaiting period may apply\nOnly full-time employees eligible\nWork Remotely:\nNo"
