   "Job Title": "Java Developer",
   "Job Description": "Travel Required: None\nRequisition Type: Regular\n\nWe are GDIT. The people supporting and securing some of the most complex government, defense, and intelligence projects across the country. We ensure today is safe and tomorrow is smarter. Our work has meaning and impact on the world around us, but also on us, and that’s important.\n\nGDIT is your place. You make it your own by embracing autonomy, seizing opportunity, and being trusted to deliver your best every day.\n\nWe think. We act. We deliver. There is no challenge we can’t turn into opportunity. And our work depends on a TS/SCI level cleared Software Developer joining our team to support our Intelligence customer in Reston, VA.\n\nIn support of a DoD customer, the software developer shall develop software programs and databases to collect, store, forward and disseminate sensor datasets to include:\n\nSupport data storage, data discovery, exploitation and analysis that are compatible with existing SCS, ATI, and mission partner tools (i.e. Database designs, use Database Design Document)\nDevelop scripts and software tools to manipulate data and move it automatically between networks and folders.\nSanitize correlation data\nDevelop scripts to evaluate user dataset development\nDevelop API/GUI and data sources\nThe software developer shall use an iterative, incremental, or other agreed upon system engineering processes to design, develop, deploy, document, and certify and accredit TPED IT systems.\nThe software developer shall define and document a general Software Development Plan (SDP) delineating the software development approach for the computer software efforts to be performed IAW (IEEE/EIA) Std. 12207.0, to include:\nDefining the proposed or established life cycle model and the processes and Plans and Procedures Table 1 used as part of that model IAW (IEEE/EIA) Std. 12207.0:\nIdentify the specific standards, methods, tools, actions, strategies, and responsibilities associated with software development and qualification\nDocument all processes applicable to the system to be acquired, including the Primary, Supporting, and Organizational life cycle processes, at a minimum, CMMI Level 2 processes.\nEnsure consistency with the processes proposed by the developers; adhere to characteristics, organizational processes etc.\nWill contain a level of information sufficient to be utilized as full guidance for the developers. (i.e. specific standards, methods, tools, actions, reuse strategy, and responsibility associated with the development and qualification of all requirements, including safety and security).\nOperate in customer environment\nPrepare as required, all source code and associated concept papers associated with software, test related software, and applications developed under this order\nMay perform special project or duties as required\n\nRequired Qualifications :\n\nBA/BS/MS\nTS/SCI and CI Polygraph Eligible\n10+ years’ experience\nMinimum 8570 compliant IAT Level 2\n#GDITPriority We are GDIT. The people supporting some of the most complex government, defense, and intelligence projects across the country. We deliver. Bringing the expertise needed to understand and advance critical missions. We transform. Shifting the ways clients invest in, integrate, and innovate technology solutions. We ensure today is safe and tomorrow is smarter. We are there. On the ground, beside our clients, in the lab, and everywhere in between. Offering the technology transformations, strategy, and mission services needed to get the job done.\n\nGDIT is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or veteran status, or any other protected class."
