   "Job Title": "Software Engineer",
   "Job Description": "Full Stack Developer\n\nPosition Summary\n\nWe are looking for an experienced full-stack developer, a team player who's passionate about technology, learning and problem solving.\n\nYou will join our UI team, owning end to end responsibility for our web platform and infrastructure, and be involved in building our roadmap by researching product behavior and usage.\n\nWe’re working in a fast-paced environment, daily shipping new features and improved infrastructure, working closely with all teams across the company mainly the product, data, DevOps and QA teams.\n\nRole and Responsibilities\nDesign, code and manage our web platform using industry best practices focusing on quality, performance, and delivery.\nWrite well-crafted, well-tested, readable, maintainable code.\nMake sure our team’s development effort fulfills its purpose, taking our product and infrastructure to the next level.\nParticipate in code reviews, evaluate implementations and provide feedback to ensure code quality and distribute knowledge.\nJob Requirements\n\nAt least 3 years of experience in UX/UI – must!\n\nExperience both in Frontend and Backend development\n\nExcellent understanding of Angular7 framework, TypeScript, Node.js, npm, HTML5/CSS3/ECMAScript6.\n\nExperience with cloud and multi-tenancy development.\n\nBSc. in Computer Science or equivalent.\n\nExperience in the AngularJS (Advantage).\n\nExperience as web architect (Advantage).\n\nExperience with Java/J2EE server side development, Spring Web MVC (Advantage)\n\nFamiliarity with WCAG best practices. (Advantage)\n\nExcellent communication skills.\n\nExperience with scalable API based agent or service oriented software architecture.\n\n*************************************************************************************************************\n\nThe above statements describe the general nature and level of work being performed by people assigned to this job. They are not intended to be an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential job functions. If you need assistance or an accommodation due to disability please contact your recruitment partner.\n\n*************************************************************************************************************"
