   "Job Title": "DevOps Engineer",
   "Job Description": "Job Requisition ID #\n20WD42374\n\nPosition Overview :\n\nAutodesk is looking for Site Reliability Engineer to join our talented Operations Engineering and Architecture team. If you are a reliability engineer or DevOps engineer, we want you to join!Autodesk, the leading Design and Engineering software company, is transitioning to the cloud! As a global leader in 3D design, engineering, and entertainment software, Autodesk helps people imagine, design, and create a better world. Autodesk accelerates better design through an unparalleled depth of experience and a broad portfolio of software to give customers the power to solve their design, business, and environmental challenges. In addition to designers, architects, engineers, and media and entertainment professionals, Autodesk helps students, educators, and casual creators unlock their creative ideas through user-friendly applications.\n\nWhat drives you? Are you passionate about AI, Automation, Innovation and Cloud Ops technologies? Come work with the team and use your expertise and skills to design, build and support the platforms. You will be working closely with the engineering and enterprise application teams to ensure systems are secure, highly available and scalable. Your experience and scripting skills will help you automate scaling and management of server resources and implement code for zero-downtime deployments and to facilitate DevOps practices. This position offers an outstanding opportunity for a unique individual who possesses solid scripting background\n\nResponsibilities :\nResponsible for defining systems architecture of Cloud Hosted enterprise solutions\nImplement Continuous Delivery mechanism\nAutomate the manual processes using suitable scripting language\nClearly document architecture & infrastructure\nDefine & adhere to rigorous change management policies\nDevelop appropriate technical diagramming to show interconnectivity of interacting systems and networks.\nDrive and improve performance, scalability, security and availability\nMonitor, recommend and implement tools\nOptimize scaling/performance of networks, servers, monitoring and storage systems.\nImplement preventative and corrective measures\nLiaise with hosting partners to troubleshoot problems.\nPerform root cause analysis of critical outages\nResponsible for driving the process for efficient (and complete/secure) backup and restore\nMinimum Qualifications :\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering or a related field, plus 7 years of progressive professional experience\n2-4 years’ experience in Java programming\nAWS 2+ years of experience with knowledge on AWS technologies like EC2, Lambda, ELB, S3, CloudWatch, IAM, KMS, VPC, Dynamo DB, RDS.\nDevOps experience, with automation experience with configuration tools and management tools.\nScripting skills - Python and shell scripting.\nProblem Solving Ability – Ability to analyze and resolve infrastructure issues and deployment issues.\nDevelop scalable Cloud solutions\nExperience with creation and maintenance of Hosting Environments\nExperience with Maven, Jenkins and GitHub\nExperience with Apache, Tomcat, Jetty or similar servers.\nUnderstanding, diagnostics, troubleshooting of Java based applications\nExperience with automation or scripting (e.g. Shell/Python/Perl/Ruby)\nExperience with Linux and Windows operating systems\nKnowledge of networking and security concepts\nStrong written and verbal skills\n#LinkedIn\n\nAt Autodesk, we're building a diverse workplace and an inclusive culture to give more people the chance to imagine, design, and make a better world. Autodesk is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status or any other legally protected characteristic. We also consider for employment all qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with applicable law.\n\nAre you an existing contractor or consultant with Autodesk? Please search for open jobs and apply internally (not on this external site). If you have any questions or require support, contact Autodesk Careers."
