   "Job Description": "About the company:\nRoadMetrics provides an accurate, efficient and portable solution to all road problems. Our smartphone application provides detailed road assessments in real-time using our artificial intelligence algorithm, thus helping governments and private firms to expedite road maintenance.\nAbout the internship/job:\nSelected intern's day-to-day responsibilities include: 1. Design, implement, and evaluate novel computer vision algorithms and models 2. Work on large-scale datasets, creating scalable, robust, and accurate computer vision systems 3. Build end-to-end data pipelines to handle and manage large amounts of data 4. Go through the images manually sometimes and label them, debug models or interact with clients to create a custom model for them 5. Work in Python, Open CV, and deep learning frameworks like TensorFlow, Keras\nWho can apply:\nOnly those students or freshers can apply who:\nare available for full time (in-office) internship\nhave relevant skills and interests\ncan start the internship between 9th Dec'20 and 13th Jan'21\nare available for duration of 3 months\nhave already graduated or are currently in any year of study\nFemales willing to start/restart their career may also apply\nNumber of internships/jobs available: 1\nCategories: Computer Vision,Machine Learning,Computer Science,Engineering,Data Science"
