   "Job Title": "Java Developer",
   "Job Description": "About*\nWe are seeking a skilled candidate who has solid development experience and is well established with the below technical areas. Are you passionate and interested in helping to build a Product Development department? Are you ready to be directly involved in the creation of new products on a daily basis, in addition to being a key person in coaching, and helping to create our best practices around the development of software? Are you personable and good at communicating your opinions clearly, completely, passionately? Are you looking for a fast-paced, collaborative environment? This could be the position for you! We expect the average candidate for this position to be 5-10 years into their career.\nResponsibilities*\nWork with junior developers to establish and implement project tracking methodology\nWork with the team to prioritize projects\nUse your background and experience to help develop architecture standards and approaches that will exist on all projects\nHelp to create systems for maintaining production products\nBalance your desire to innovate with new platforms and tools, against your desire for scalability and maintainability with a small team\nHelp develop user stories by meeting with and discussing projects with stakeholders\nCoach and mentor developers using your core values of development and architecture\nA love for simple but powerful user interface and user experience, even when creating line-of-business software\nTechnical Skills*\n.Net Core/C#\nDomain Driven Design architecture\nT-SQL, particularly SQL Server\nBlazor (Web Assembly) or proficiency in JS data binding libraries such as React, Angular, or Vue\nEntity Framework Core and/or other ORM libraries\nCSS/Sass\nJavascript and common JS UI libraries\nFamiliarity with common UI libraries/specifications, such as Bootstrap or Material\nFamiliarity with other persistence methodologies such as graph, time-series, and schemaless\nSignalR, WebAPI\nVisual Studio\nGithub and common source control best practices\nDocker\nJob Type: Full-time\n\nPay: From $90,000.00 per year\n\nBenefits:\n401(k)\nDental insurance\nHealth insurance\nPaid time off\nVision insurance\nSchedule:\n8 hour shift\nMonday to Friday\nExperience:\nIT: 5 years (Required)\nLocation:\nEnglewood, CO 80112 (Required)\nWork Location:\nOne location\nVisa Sponsorship Potentially Available:\nNo: Not providing sponsorship for this job\nWork Remotely:\nNo"
